# Always give a verified link (HARD)

**Owner 2026-08-14:** *"i need a link — give me one every single time."* Andrew reviewed a Returns page for 15 minutes that had none of the changes on it.

## Every turn that touches `shopify-build/**`

End the reply with a working link. No link = the task is not finished.

## Use the primary domain — NOT myshopify.com

```
✅ https://barreletics.com/pages/returns?preview_theme_id=187144929571
❌ https://barreletics.myshopify.com/pages/returns?preview_theme_id=187144929571
```

`barreletics.myshopify.com` **301-redirects to `barreletics.com` and drops the preview parameter**, silently serving the **live** theme. The CLI prints the myshopify URL — do not paste it. Rewrite it to the primary domain and append the page path.

Tell Andrew to reload once if it looks unchanged: the first hit sets the preview cookie and may still render live.

## NEVER truncate push output

```
❌ shopify theme push … | tail -3      # hides the error banner
✅ shopify theme push … 2>&1           # read all of it
```

The CLI prints a **success box even when a file was rejected**. On 2026-08-14 every `page-returns.liquid` push failed schema validation for five straight attempts while the banner said success. Read the whole output and look for `─ error ─`.

## Schema gotcha that caused it

Shopify rejects a blank default outright. **Omit the key** to mean empty.

```
❌ { "type": "text", "id": "x", "label": "X", "default": "" }
✅ { "type": "text", "id": "x", "label": "X" }
```

## One `--only` per file

Repeated or space-separated patterns silently drop files. Push separately and verify each.

```
❌ --only "sections/a.liquid" "templates/b.json"
✅ --only "sections/a.liquid"   then   --only "templates/b.json"
```

## Verify before linking, then say so

Curl the draft and grep for a string you added **and** one you removed:

```bash
curl -s -c j.txt -o /dev/null -L "https://barreletics.com/?preview_theme_id=187144929571"
curl -s -b j.txt -o p.html -L "https://barreletics.com/<path>?preview_theme_id=187144929571"
rg -F -c "string I added" p.html      # expect 1
rg -F -c "string I removed" p.html    # expect 0
```

The cookie jar is required — a single cold request serves the live theme.

